From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] test-init: clean up the early-failure crash from Gentoo's sleep too

Test images crash 'sleep 10000' on purpose at early boot
(early-failure.conf) and remove the report once no crash test needs it.
The cleanup looked for reports named "coreutils", Google's coreutils
being one multicall program; NickelOS Unified runs Gentoo's coreutils, one
program per command, so the report is named "sleep" and stayed.

---
--- a/upstart/test-init/early-failure-cleanup.conf
+++ b/upstart/test-init/early-failure-cleanup.conf
@@ -31,11 +31,12 @@
   # coreutils crash.
 
   # Find crashes:
-  #  * from 'coreutils'
+  #  * from 'coreutils' (NickelOS: or 'sleep', Gentoo's coreutils having one
+  #    program per command)
   #  * during early boot
   #  * invoked as 'sleep 10000'
   # And remove them
-  find /var/spool/crash/ -maxdepth 1 -name "coreutils.*.meta" \
+  find /var/spool/crash/ -maxdepth 1 \( -name "coreutils.*.meta" -o -name "sleep.*.meta" \) \
       -exec grep -l upload_var_is_early_boot=true {} + | \
   while IFS= read -r file; do
     proclog="${file%.meta}.proclog"
